WEBVTT

00:00.040 --> 00:04.560
So I'm going to show you the steps that we usually do in the industry to do data analysis.

00:04.600 --> 00:07.400
So the first phase is the EDA projects.

00:07.400 --> 00:10.120
Usually the first step is we explore the database.

00:10.120 --> 00:12.720
So what are the tables and the columns inside it.

00:12.720 --> 00:16.360
Then we explore the dimensions inside the tables.

00:16.360 --> 00:20.400
And then we explore different dates to understand the range of the data.

00:20.440 --> 00:26.000
And then we try to explore the measures like how many customers, how many orders, how many products.

00:26.000 --> 00:29.280
And then in the next step we do something called magnitude analysis.

00:29.280 --> 00:32.280
It is just we group up something by another thing.

00:32.280 --> 00:38.520
So you take one dimension and one measure and combine them like find the number of orders by products,

00:38.520 --> 00:41.240
the total sales by customers.

00:41.240 --> 00:43.320
So it's like we are combining two things together.

00:43.320 --> 00:46.000
And the last step is we start doing ranking.

00:46.000 --> 00:49.160
So top customers, top products, top categories and so on.

00:49.160 --> 00:54.760
So those are generally the steps that we use to explore any data sets for any industry.

00:54.760 --> 00:59.240
I worked in five different industries and I end up using always those tips.

00:59.280 --> 01:04.440
Now after that we start doing some advanced analytical stuff, like for example, the changes over time

01:04.440 --> 01:07.520
in order to see how things evolves over the time.

01:07.520 --> 01:12.680
We have to learn to do cumulative analyses to show how values build up over time.

01:12.680 --> 01:18.160
And of course, very famous one performance analysis in order to compare things together and another

01:18.160 --> 01:23.280
type of analysis, we have the part to whole to explain how each part contributes to the total.

01:23.280 --> 01:26.720
And this can help us to understand the importance of the data.

01:26.720 --> 01:32.400
And another type is data segmentations, where you can group up and segment the data of, for example,

01:32.400 --> 01:33.840
the users, their products.

01:33.840 --> 01:38.360
And of course, another type we do is reporting and this is a classical one that we do.

01:38.360 --> 01:43.360
So we build one view in order to answer multiple business questions in one go.

01:43.360 --> 01:46.120
And of course you can do the whole thing using SQL.

01:46.120 --> 01:48.280
So now this is the whole roadmap for the projects.

01:48.280 --> 01:50.680
And of course we're going to do everything step by step.

01:50.760 --> 01:52.720
And we're going to start with the EDA project.

01:52.760 --> 01:53.400
Let's go.
